Read the Update as an instruction the Actor would have to follow. If it asks the Actor to make several choices, consider what supports each one. For each choice the Update would change, what could the Actor see at that point, and how much does that cue settle? The wording of a single task can settle a choice when it gives an explicit requirement. When a cue leaves several actions reasonable, what evidence supports requiring one, preferring it, or leaving the choice open?

